"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":10,"usage":null},{"content":"I checked, and my messaging app is currently unable to send MMS messages. What should I try next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":11,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:27.070872","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":11,"usage":{"completion_tokens":23,"prompt_tokens":2613}},{"content":"Thank you for checking. Since your messaging app cannot send MMS messages, let’s proceed with some troubleshooting steps. First, we need to ensure your phone has both cellular service and mobile data enabled, as these are required for MMS.\n\nPlease check your phone’s status bar and let me know:\n- Do you see signal bars (indicating cellular service)?\n- Is there a mobile data icon (such as 4G, LTE, 5G, etc.) visible?\n\nIf you’re unsure, you can use the check_status_bar diagnostic action on your phone and share the results with me. This will help us determine the next steps.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":12,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:28.830043","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":12,"usage":{"completion_tokens":129,"prompt_tokens":6830}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":13,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:29.584479","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_s57hyxMLcu9pdnXCJtyFDW1u","name":"check_status_bar","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":13,"usage":{"completion_tokens":12,"prompt_tokens":2769}},{"content":"Status Bar: ✈️ Airplane Mode | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":14,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:29.584887","tool_call_id":"call_s57hyxMLcu9pdnXCJtyFDW1u","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":14,"usage":null},{"content":"I checked my status bar, and it shows that Airplane Mode is enabled. There are no signal bars or mobile data icons visible. What should I do next?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":15,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:30.770783","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":15,"usage":{"completion_tokens":35,"prompt_tokens":2802}},{"content":"Airplane Mode disables all wireless connections, including cellular service and mobile data, which are required for sending MMS messages.\n\nPlease turn off Airplane Mode on your phone. You can usually do this by:\n- Swiping down from the top of your screen to open the quick settings panel.\n- Tapping the Airplane Mode icon to disable it.\n\nOnce Airplane Mode is off, check if your signal bars and mobile data icons reappear. Then, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if the issue is resolved or if you still experience problems.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":16,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:32.354916","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":16,"usage":{"completion_tokens":114,"prompt_tokens":6998}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":17,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:33.238675","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_EiNY1Pc6oM3c39ds01KZHTVW","name":"toggle_airplane_mode","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":17,"usage":{"completion_tokens":13,"prompt_tokens":2955}},{"content":"Airplane Mode is now OFF.\nStatus Bar: 📶¹ Poor | 2G | 📱 Data Enabled | 🔋 80%","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":18,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:33.239131","tool_call_id":"call_EiNY1Pc6oM3c39ds01KZHTVW","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":18,"usage":null},{"content":"I’ve turned off Airplane Mode. Now, I see a signal bar with “2G” and the data icon is enabled. Should I try sending an MMS again, or is there something else I should check first?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":19,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:34.690765","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":19,"usage":{"completion_tokens":47,"prompt_tokens":3004}},{"content":"Thank you for the update. Since your phone is currently connected to a 2G network, this may be the reason MMS is not working—MMS typically requires at least a 3G connection.\n\nPlease check your phone’s network mode preference and, if it is set to 2G or 3G only, change it to allow 4G or 5G if available. You can do this by running the check_network_mode_preference diagnostic action on your phone. Let me know what it shows, and I’ll guide you on how to update it if needed.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":20,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:36.255692","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":20,"usage":{"completion_tokens":119,"prompt_tokens":7163}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":21,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:37.097768","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{},"id":"call_YNGiLmj3dZ5i5AndzWyGfIbi","name":"check_network_mode_preference","requestor":"user_simulator"}],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":21,"usage":{"completion_tokens":14,"prompt_tokens":3174}},{"content":"Network Mode Preference: 2g_only","native_cost":null,"participant":"tool_environment","reasoning":null,"requestor":"user_simulator","role":"tool","sequence":22,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:37.098204","tool_call_id":"call_YNGiLmj3dZ5i5AndzWyGfIbi","tool_calls":[],"tool_error":false,"turn_index":22,"usage":null},{"content":"My phone’s network mode preference is currently set to 2G only. What should I do to change this so I can try sending MMS messages again?","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":23,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:38.081974","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":23,"usage":{"completion_tokens":33,"prompt_tokens":3204}},{"content":"To improve your connectivity and enable MMS functionality, please change your network mode preference to allow 4G or 5G connections. \n\nOn your phone, set the network mode preference to “4G/5G preferred” (or a similar option, such as “LTE/5G auto” or “4G/3G/2G auto”). This will allow your phone to connect to faster networks that support MMS.\n\nAfter changing the network mode, wait a moment for your phone to connect to the new network. Once you see 4G, LTE, or 5G in your status bar, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if it works or if you encounter any issues.","native_cost":0.0,"participant":"evaluated_agent","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"assistant","sequence":24,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:40.061669","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[],"tool_error":null,"turn_index":24,"usage":{"completion_tokens":145,"prompt_tokens":7319}},{"content":null,"native_cost":0.0,"participant":"user_simulator","reasoning":null,"requestor":null,"role":"user","sequence":25,"thinking_blocks":null,"timestamp":"2026-10-20T17:44:41.108752","tool_call_id":null,"tool_calls":[{"arguments":{"mode":"4g_5g_preferred"},"id":"cal